    "full_width_text_xyfhCe": {
      "type": "full-width-text",
      "name": "Full Width Text",
      "settings": {
        "headline": "ONDA PRO",
        "large_headline": "",
        "copy": "<p><strong>The Science</strong></p><p>OndaPro uses microwave energy at 2.45 GHz, a frequency that selectively targets the dermis and subcutaneous fat with a level of depth precision that radio frequency and ultrasound-based devices cannot reliably achieve.</p><p>At the tissue level, two distinct processes occur simultaneously.</p><p>The first is an immediate thermal effect. Controlled collagen denaturation causes the existing collagen network to contract, producing visible tightening from the first session.</p><p>The second is a regenerative cascade. Thermal injury triggers a wound-healing response, upregulating heat shock proteins involved in collagen synthesis and, critically, downregulating matrix metalloproteinases, the enzymes responsible for collagen breakdown.</p><p>This second point matters. Most technologies stimulate new collagen production. Fewer also reduce collagen degradation. OndaPro does both, which translates to net collagen gain rather than simple turnover.</p><p><strong>Depth-Specific Targeting</strong></p><p>The system's handpiece design allows for tissue-level selectivity. Superficial settings address dermal tightening and skin quality, while deeper settings target subcutaneous adipose tissue for fat reduction and cellulite improvement. This makes it possible to treat skin laxity and localized fat deposits, including hormonally driven accumulation in the flanks, abdomen, and arms, within the same session.</p><p></p>"
      }
    },
