    "full_width_text_cVgGMH": {
      "type": "full-width-text",
      "name": "Full Width Text",
      "settings": {
        "headline": "",
        "large_headline": "",
        "copy": "<p><strong>What Treatment Is Like</strong></p><p>Sessions last approximately 20 minutes. No numbing is required, though pre-treatment analgesia is recommended as heat accumulation toward the end of the session can become intense. Most patients tolerate this well. Results are visible immediately and continue to improve over the following weeks as the regenerative response matures.</p><p><strong>What I Am Seeing Clinically</strong></p><p>This technology is already changing how I approach certain cases. For patients with early skin laxity and good baseline health, strong nutrition, an active lifestyle, and minimal subcutaneous fat, I am achieving results I previously could only obtain in the operating room using subdermal energy devices under anesthesia. No recovery. No downtime. Better patient experience.</p><p>For this population specifically, OndaPro is not a compromise. It is, in many cases, the superior option.</p><p><strong>Who Should Consider This</strong></p><p>I encourage patients to think about OndaPro as a proactive tool, not just a corrective one. The best outcomes in aging skin come from intervening early, before laxity becomes pronounced. If you are in your 40s or 50s, maintaining your body well, and beginning to notice early changes in skin texture or contour, this is precisely the window where this technology performs best.</p><p>It is also well suited for targeted concerns including menopausal fat redistribution, post-weight-loss skin changes, arm laxity, and abdominal skin quality following pregnancy or significant lifestyle changes.</p><p>The goal is to keep patients out of the operating room, not by settling for less, but by having a tool that is genuinely effective at the right stage of intervention. OndaPro is that tool.</p>"
      }
    },
